      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking that init_s2mpu_driver() (and its sysmmu counterpart) should call __pkvm_register_iommu_driver() and pass a pointer to the pkvm_iommu_driver struct directly. Alternatively you could pass that pointer to __pkvm_iommu_driver_init() directly and have it call __pkvm_register_iommu_driver() unconditionally?\n\nAlso, do we really need this patch for now or is it only going to be useful when we modularize everything?",
